scan_for_matches_rs is a Rust port of scan_for_matches.

Original program
  scan_for_matches: A Program to Scan Nucleotide or Protein Sequences for
  Matching Patterns.  Ross Overbeek, MCS, Argonne National Laboratory,
  Argonne, IL 60439, USA.  Source: The SEED
  (https://www.theseed.org/servers/downloads/scan_for_matches.tgz;
  https://blog.theseed.org/servers/2010/07/scan-for-matches.html).
  Paper: Dsouza M, Larsen N, Overbeek R. 1997. Searching for patterns in
  genomic data. Trends in Genetics 13:497-498.

The original source package has no license statement.  The author of this
port could not reach the original authors.  So:

* The pattern language, the search method and the program design are the
  work of the original authors.  The Rust code follows the C code
  (scan_for_matches.c, ggpunit.c) closely.
* README.original and the original test files (tests/data/test_dna_input,
  test_dna_patterns, test_prot_input, test_prot_patterns, test_output) are
  copies of files of the original package and belong to their authors.
* The BSD 3-Clause License in LICENSE covers only the new work of this
  port.  It gives no rights in the original work.

If you are an author of the original program and want a change here,
please open an issue on https://github.com/xavierzheng/scan_for_matches_rs.
